      {
        "id": 20587,
        "name": "rams66",
        "username": "rams66",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/e19adc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-17T06:12:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Christopher&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Christopher\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Since it’s been brought up, our intention with expansions is to not have them come in little booster packs or anything like that.  Rather, you’d get another significant chunk of cards - each standard expansion will have 2 heroes, 4 villains, and 2 environments.  I say “standard expansions”, as we have some plans in the works as well for some “mega-expansions”, as well as other nifty tricks and such.  I assure you, we have plans . . .</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>that is a pretty awesome way to release an expansion. a cool thing to release with the expansion or perhaps alone, could be custom printed rubber bands to match the decks (so you can keep them together). similar to this <a href=\"http://www.aerorubber.com/printedbands.htm\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.aerorubber.com/printedbands.htm</a> , or perhaps custom tabbed dividers for those deck boxes that hold around 175 or so cards.</p>",
